2025-02-05 16:27:39,776 INFO Task 514fd9e9-0fa7-434f-86b3-e573ef842624 result: {'model': 'model1', 'real_model': 'claude', 'summary': 'Here are the key findings from the paper summarized in 5 lines:\n\n1. Using single-nucleus RNA sequencing and spatial transcriptomics of liver samples from 17 COVID-19 patients, the study identified SARS-CoV-2 RNA-positive hepatocytes exhibiting expression patterns similar to infected lung epithelial cells.\n\n2. COVID-19 livers showed extensive cellular changes including hepatocellular injury, ductular reaction, vascular expansion, and fibrogenesis, despite absence of clinical liver injury symptoms.\n\n3. The study discovered Kupffer cell proliferation and erythrocyte progenitors in human liver for the first time, similar to responses seen in mouse liver injury and sepsis models.\n\n4. Endothelial cell composition was dramatically altered in COVID-19 livers, along with extensive changes in reactive cholangiocytes and mesenchymal cells showing profibrogenic activation.\n\n5. The findings reveal previously unknown liver pathology in COVID-19 and suggest potential long-term implications for liver health in recovered patients, while providing a comprehensive atlas for future research.', 'status': 'success', 'model_id': 'claude_7165', 'request_id': '000a1e96-8ed5-4091-923b-6a754a5f47b8'}
